@startuml
title Figure 10 — Deployment and communication topology
top to bottom direction
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 45

node "Operator device" as Device {
  artifact "Web browser" as Browser
}

node "Docker Compose / Linux host" as Host {
  node "web service / container" as Web {
    artifact "React static UI\n(+ reverse proxy in remote demo)" as React
  }

  node "api service / container" as Api {
    artifact "Spring Boot modular monolith" as Spring
    artifact "Offline adapters\nStaticPolicyAdapter +\nDeterministicAnalysisStub" as Offline
  }

  database "db service / container\nPostgreSQL + pgvector" as DB
}

cloud "Optional external AI provider" as Provider

Browser --> Web : HTTP localhost\nHTTPS remote demo
Web --> Api : HTTP/JSON /api/*\nCompose private network
Api --> DB : JDBC / PostgreSQL\nTCP 5432 private network
Api ..> Provider : HTTPS provider API\nonly when configured
Api --> Offline : in-process baseline path

Web -[hidden]down-> Api
Api -[hidden]down-> DB
DB -[hidden]right-> Provider

note bottom of Host
  Baseline communication is synchronous request/response.
  No WebSocket, broker, FIFO, Redis, or separate identity service is assumed.
  The database port remains private to the Compose network.
end note
@enduml
